Turn a broad AI answer into a useful learning agenda — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Request
New finance operations analyst; 30 minutes; learn receipt, classification, routing, approval, posting. Question: "Teach me everything about finance automation." Deliberately flawed AI draft: "Routing an invoice to treasury means it is approved for payment. Approval can be skipped because routing establishes authority." Internal policy and vendor documentation unavailable.
Task
A colleague asks 'teach me everything about finance automation.' Build a short learning agenda for understanding invoice routing, with a clear stopping point.
Actions
	1	Identify the decision the learner is preparing for: explaining a process, not authorizing payment.
	2	Ask AI to narrow the topic to the five named stages and give three follow-up questions.
	3	Ask which claims require company policy or tool documentation and mark these as unknown.
	4	Correct the seeded routing/approval confusion and map the five stages in order.
	5	Write what you should be able to explain after 30 minutes and what will remain out of scope.
Output
Rewritten question; three follow-ups; scope exclusions; source needs; corrected concept map; learning stop condition.
